<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Bronze Angel's care voucher is worth 3,000 GHS, not 5,000.

        Mirrors hc-crowdfund-app's V9__bronze_voucher_value_correction.sql, which corrects the same
        figure at the source (voucher_value_minor 500000 -> 300000). That platform owns the pledge;
        this table is display-only, so the only thing that has to happen here is that the two agree.

        Only the tier is repriced there, not pledge.voucher_value_minor — that is a snapshot taken
        at pledge time, so existing Bronze backers keep the 5,000 GHS voucher they were promised.
        Nothing in this table is a snapshot of anything, so there is no equivalent concern here.

        A NEW changelog, not an edit to 20260730190400. Liquibase checksums applied changesets, so
        changing one in place fails validation on the next boot and takes the application down — and
        it would not update anything anyway, because an applied changeset never re-runs. On a fresh
        database the seed inserts 5000.00 and this changeset immediately corrects it; the end state
        is the same either way.
    -->

    <changeSet id="20260804090000-1" author="abofonsa" contextFilter="!test">
        <comment>Bronze Angel voucher: 5000.00 -> 3000.00 GHS.</comment>
        <update tableName="pledge_tier_teaser">
            <column name="voucher_value" valueNumeric="3000.00"/>
            <where>code = 'BRONZE'</where>
        </update>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
        contextFilter="!test" for the same reason 20260730190400 carries it: the row this updates is
        seed content, and the seed does not load in the test context. Without the filter this would
        be a no-op update against an empty table on every test run.
    -->

</databaseChangeLog>
